1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,878
You cut your hand on a sharp stone.

2
00:00:02,828 --> 00:00:04,947
It barely bleeds.

3
00:00:04,947 --> 00:00:10,328
Before antibiotics, even a cut that small could lead to a deadly infection.

4
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:17,328
Ancient healers dressed wounds with honey, used ant jaws as stitches, and drilled teeth with stone tools.

5
00:00:17,328 --> 00:00:19,960
Some even drilled into skulls.

6
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,078
New bone around those holes shows that some patients survived.

7
00:00:24,078 --> 00:00:29,486
At Shanidar Cave, a Neanderthal lived for years after serious injuries.

8
00:00:29,486 --> 00:00:32,644
Someone may have helped him eat and get around.

9
00:00:32,644 --> 00:00:35,289
Now imagine that cut again.

10
00:00:35,289 --> 00:00:39,407
This time, someone kneels beside you and takes your hand.

11
00:00:39,407 --> 00:00:44,513
Maybe the oldest medicine began when someone saw you were hurt and chose to stay.

